867
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:37,320
with a very visible flame

868
00:25:37,320 --> 00:25:39,440
in daylight. So make sure

869
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:40,400
you read the directions

870
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,480
that come with your stove,

871
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:43,960
because a common accident

872
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:45,160
that happens with alcohol

873
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:46,600
stoves is when somebody

874
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:48,960
tries to refuel the stove

875
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,040
while it's still burning

876
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:51,680
or the burner is hot. So

877
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:52,960
make sure that it's out

878
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:54,040
and the burner is cool

879
00:25:54,040 --> 00:25:55,440
to the touch before you

880
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:57,680
refuel the stove. Once again,

881
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:59,080
folks go to the guide

882
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:00,200
to save scouting. read

883
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,520
that policy and see if

884
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:03,360
I've got it right. And

885
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:04,400
the last email for this

886
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,200
week is this question: What

887
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,960
is the maximum recommended

888
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:09,800
weight for backpacks? Some

889
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:10,800
of the old

890
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:12,320
scouters in the troop

891
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:13,760
keep telling me that one

892
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:15,760
third body weight is

893
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:17,440
the maximum, And I find

894
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:19,040
references online telling me

895
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:20,480
one quarter body weight

896
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,040
is maximum and I'd appreciate

897
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:24,240
your wisdom on this. Well,

898
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:25,120
I got to tell you the

899
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,400
percentage of body weight is

900
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,480
not a very good measure

901
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,720
when it comes to figuring

902
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:30,320
out what the maximum

903
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,240
weight of a backpack

904
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:33,120
ought to be, If you think

905
00:26:33,120 --> 00:26:34,480
about this. so one third

906
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:35,600
or one quarter body weight

907
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,680
means 150 pound person

908
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:39,640
could carry up to 50 pounds

909
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,960
And to me that's

910
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,360
way way too heavy. It's

911
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:44,080
much more than it needs to be.

912
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,960
My pack usually weighs

913
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:48,880
in around 25 to 35 pounds

914
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,680
And 35 pounds is pretty heavy

915
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,840
for for a two night weekend.

916
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:54,400
If I was a lot more serious

917
00:26:54,400 --> 00:26:55,560
about it, I paid more attention

918
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:56,600
to it, I could trim about

919
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:57,960
five pounds off of the

920
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,080
weight that I carry, But

921
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:00,200
I'm reasonably happy

922
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:02,000
getting it to in that

923
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,320
30 pound area. Scouts

924
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:05,480
in my experience are all

925
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:06,480
over the map with what

926
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:07,480
they're able to carry

927
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:09,120
comfortably. 30 pounds

928
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:10,480
is not necessarily too much

929
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:12,760
for a small, framed younger scout.

930
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,200
Now some smaller scouts

931
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,840
are going to be really taxed

932
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:17,160
trying to carry that much

933
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,480
And I've had much bigger

934
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,280
and more and older scouts

935
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:22,440
who have real difficulty

936
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,640
carrying a backpack.

937
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:24,880
It just seems to get under

938
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:26,120
their skin and it's very,

939
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:27,680
very difficult for them to do

940
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:29,000
And this is why, when we go

941
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,360
backpacking, we go

942
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:32,520
backpacking by patrols.

943
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:33,440
You know the whole troop is

944
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,640
there, but the patrols

945
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,680
sticks together.

946
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,040
They share their food,

947
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,680
They share their cooking gear,

948
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:40,960
stoves, tents, and the guys

949
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,120
who are more capable of

950
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:43,760
carrying more weight will

951
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:45,480
usually be very happy

952
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:46,920
to do that if somebody

953
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,680
is having trouble in their patrol.

954
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:49,960
So I know there's a lot

955
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:50,960
of advice out there that

956
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:52,520
talks about a percentage

957
00:27:52,520 --> 00:27:53,800
of body weight as being

958
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:55,360
a measure for the maximum,

959
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:56,760
But, like I said, there are

960
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:58,320
so many different situations

961
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,520
and so many different types

962
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,160
of scouts that I would not

963
00:28:01,160 --> 00:28:02,760
use that as a rule of thumb.

964
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:03,920
The way that it works best

965
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,880
for us has been to stay

966
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:08,680
in that 25 to 35 pound area

967
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:09,880
and to make sure that

968
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:10,960
everybody sticks together

969
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:11,960
as patrol,

970
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:12,960
And it usually seems

971
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:15,080
to work out just fine that way.

